by nicolas-grekas at 2026-02-14T13:38:09Z

This can give nice visual hints when the terminal is in the background, by allowing the icon of the term to report the status. This is supported eg by:
- Windows Terminal / ConEmu → progress appears on the taskbar icon
- WezTerm → tab and window progress
- some Linux terminals (VTE-based) → tab indicators

<img width="141" height="112" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3f7da1bf-2a3c-4a1e-bd72-e6fca5b7a374" />

<img width="136" height="87" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a8eb52b1-9111-4fbb-8ccd-b48543a71674" />

For the record, the basic form of the escape sequence is:

`ESC ] 9 ; 4 ; state ; progress ST`

Where:

- state is a number from 0 to 4 describing what to do.
- progress (optional) is a percentage 0–100.

Meaning of the state values:
- `0` Remove/hide the progress indicator
- `1` Set progress to given percentage
- `2` Set error state (often shown in red)
- `3` Indeterminate (spinner or pulsing state)
- `4` Pause/Awaiting state (optional use)

We could use state `2` when an exception occurs
and state `4` when entering interaction
for the multi progress bar case, we could use `3` and/or allow defining a master progress bar.

Maybe worth adding in this PR also? @canvural WDYT?
